WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:04.330
Stage twelve: your data, your trail.

2
00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:13.003
Everything the coach knows about Camille fits in one folder: sessions, health, nutrition, plans, reports, gear.

3
00:00:13.103 --> 00:00:18.111
Markdown files you read, edit and version in your own private repo.

4
00:00:18.961 --> 00:00:27.723
Each session opens with a small data block: English keys, SI units. A missing measurement is a missing key, never a zero.

5
00:00:27.823 --> 00:00:30.398
Below it, the coach's free text.

6
00:00:30.498 --> 00:00:33.863
After every write, validation checks the block.

7
00:00:34.713 --> 00:00:39.656
The dashboard reads these blocks from a derived SQLite database.

8
00:00:39.756 --> 00:00:46.086
Delete it: nothing is lost, it rebuilds from your files. Markdown stays the source of truth.

9
00:00:46.936 --> 00:00:52.818
One command opens the dashboard on your own machine, read-only. Nothing to install.

10
00:00:54.936 --> 00:01:01.821
You choose your source: Garmin by default, or Intervals.icu, with the source intervals option.

11
00:01:01.921 --> 00:01:09.296
With Intervals, there is no readiness score and no per-kilometre splits: the tool says so, it doesn't invent them.

12
00:01:10.146 --> 00:01:15.324
On privacy: your files stay on your machine, out of the public repository.

13
00:01:15.424 --> 00:01:23.930
But what the model reads to answer you travels, inside requests, to your IDE's model provider. That's true of any assistant.

14
00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:31.494
Older files? /arc-backfill brings them up to the contract, ten per pass, inventing nothing.

15
00:01:34.044 --> 00:01:38.091
To go further: the “workspace” page of the documentation.
